  "notes": "A few players on the courts, an otherwise peaceful outdoor setting — but how quiet is it really?\n\nThis SPL Reference measurement captures the complete soundscape from outside the tennis courts: the rhythmic impact of balls and racquets, occasional voices from the players, periods of relative calm, wind passing through the area and, every so often, an aircraft crossing far overhead.\n\nNone of these sounds necessarily dominates. Together, however, they reveal something interesting: even an environment we perceive as quiet is made from many layers of sound.\n\nA snapshot of an ordinary moment — and a reminder of just how much sound surrounds us without demanding our attention.",
